{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791598085,"nonce":"qrJtJWHkj2g7GavltUxZySXIG9E=","message":"blinc_router: the outlet was the same Stateful-per-route-version pattern as the tabs content area; moved onto a keyed row per navigation. Behaviour kept: a fresh view per navigation (also to the same path), page transitions wrap the view in a transient motion container, suspension scopes and use_router() unchanged. The outlet no longer queues a subtree rebuild; a view's signals and computeds are disposed with it. Not verified against the old outlet: it does not swap at all in the headless harness (the windowed runner installs more for statefuls), so the new tests are written from the documented behaviour, not recorded from the old code.\n\nOpen: exit playback for page transitions. exit_animation is set but never plays. Rows can now stay mounted while they leave, but MotionHandle::exit only addresses stable-keyed motions and the outlet uses transient ones on purpose (stable-keyed state accumulated across navigations). Options: a stable key per navigation (needs cleanup of RenderState::stable_motions entries, there is remove_stable_motion), or a small rotating key space (state reuse across pages). Not started.","files":null}]}